  "summary": "All 6 items in the messages queue are closed. Red flag handled first.\n\n1. Evelyn Brooks (pt-0029), RED FLAG: black stools and lightheadedness on standing while taking apixaban plus naproxen (started 10/20). Sent a stat task to pool-rn-triage (task-t0001) and an urgent portal message telling her to go to the ED now (comm-t0002). No medication changes made; that is for the prescriber/ED.\n2. Gloria Hayes (pt-0026), lisinopril 20 mg refill: NOT refilled. Most recent BMP is an outside St. Brigid result from 07/08/2026 (doc-00079): K 5.8, creatinine 1.12. No ACE inhibitor/ARB order placed. Task to PCP Dr. Okafor about mr-00281 (task-t0004). Patient told it is pending review (comm-t0005).\n3. Frank Odum (pt-0027), atorvastatin refill: NOT refilled. It conflicts with the 08/11/2026 cardiology consult (doc-00080): atorvastatin stopped for myalgias, rosuvastatin 10 mg started. Our med list still shows atorvastatin and has no rosuvastatin. Regimen left unchanged. Task to PCP about mr-00283 to reconcile the med list (task-t0007). Patient informed (comm-t0008).\n4. Lena Park (pt-0028), J. Reyes NP asked for amoxicillin-clavulanate for sinusitis: NOT ordered. The RBC-MED-04 safety check found a 03/09/2024 urgent care record (doc-00101) showing anaphylaxis within about 20 minutes of the first Augmentin dose (hives, lip/throat swelling, IM epinephrine given). The chart listed NKDA.\n   - Recorded an amoxicillin allergy: unconfirmed, high criticality, reactions coded (alg-t0010).\n   - Marked the NKDA entry inactive (alg-00023).\n   - Messaged Reyes with the finding and the protocol alternative, doxycycline 100 mg BID for 5-7 days (comm-t0012).\n   - Because Reyes's credentials are pending, also created an urgent task for Dr. Okafor to decide on and prescribe the alternative today (task-t0013). The agent did not place it.\n   - Wrote a progress note (doc-t0014).\n5. Samuel Price (pt-0030), metformin refill: renewed 1000 mg BID for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0016, replaces mr-00286). HbA1c 7.1% and eGFR 62 on 07/15/2026 meet RBC-RX-05 §2. Patient informed (comm-t0017).\n6. Marcus Webb (pt-0031), scheduling: task to pool-scheduling for a November morning BP check (task-t0019). Patient informed (comm-t0020).\n\nFollow-up for Dr. Okafor: three open tasks need your decision (Hayes lisinopril and hyperkalemia, Odum statin reconciliation, Park antibiotic choice). The Park antibiotic decision is due today.",
